DTSTART;TZID=Asia/Kolkata:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=Asia/Kolkata:20261024T193000
SUMMARY:Is metabolic care for you?
DESCRIPTION:Wondering if metabolic care is for you?\nIn men with BMI under 
 25 kg/m2\, aged 45 and over in Chennai\, Delhi and Karachi\, diabetes risk
  was 2.99 times higher in South Asians (95% CI 2.09 to 4.28) than in US wh
 ites.\nIn women with BMI under 25 kg/m2\, aged 45 and over in Chennai\, De
 lhi and Karachi\, diabetes risk was 5.27 times higher in South Asians (95%
  CI 3.64 to 7.54) than in US whites.\nPost folder: posts/run-244d0fbd0c04/
 post-0e31b93a\nPending doctor review.
STATUS:TENTATIVE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:post-92f0b86a@steer
DTSTAMP:20261019T100301Z
DTSTART;TZID=Asia/Kolkata:20261026T190000
DTEND;TZID=Asia/Kolkata:20261026T193000
SUMMARY:Will the weight come back?
DESCRIPTION:On average\, weight came back 0.4 kg a month (95% confidence in
 terval 0.3 to 0.5) after stopping weight management medicines in adults wi
 th overweight or obesity. It is an average across all weight management me
 dicines\, not only GLP-1\, and not a prediction for you.\nAmong 28 randomi
 sed controlled trials\, weight came back to the comparison group's level 1
 .4 years after stopping. This is an average across all weight management m
 edicines\, not only GLP-1\, and not a prediction for you.\nTalk to a Steer
  doctor\nPost folder: posts/run-a7cddabed62e/post-92f0b86a\nPending doctor
  review.
STATUS:TENTATIVE
END:VEVENT
